{"id":"s5","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":10,"of":14,"title":"Word order","titleHe":"סֵדֶר הַמִּלִּים","goal":"Know the default order, and what moving a word does.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Modern Hebrew is subject–verb–object, like English. Literary and biblical Hebrew often puts the verb first, which is why an old sentence can read as inverted before you've parsed it."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"הַיֶּלֶד קָרָא אֶת הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"The boy read the book. — ordinary"},{"he":"קָרָא הַיֶּלֶד אֶת הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"Read the boy the book. — literary, same meaning"},{"he":"אֶת הַסֵּפֶר קָרָא הַיֶּלֶד.","en":"It was the book the boy read. — fronted for emphasis"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Because the verb ending already tells you the person, Hebrew can drop the subject pronoun entirely in the past and future. הָלַכְתִּי is a complete sentence."}],"vocab":[{"he":"דַּוְקָא","en":"specifically, of all things","translit":"davka"},{"he":"גַּם","en":"also","translit":"gam"},{"he":"אֲפִלּוּ","en":"even","translit":"afilu"},{"he":"בִּכְלָל","en":"at all, in general","translit":"bichlal"},{"he":"כָּךְ","en":"thus, so","translit":"kach"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["suitcase","summer","tells","specifically, of all things"],"correct":3,"prompt":"דַּוְקָא","translit":"davka"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["cheap","sick, a patient","also","medicine"],"correct":2,"prompt":"גַּם","translit":"gam"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["even","ten (m.)","consequently","sometimes"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אֲפִלּוּ","translit":"afilu"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["thirty","grass","then","at all, in general"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בִּכְלָל","translit":"bichlal"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["thus, so","there","travels, rides","stands"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כָּךְ","translit":"kach"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “specifically, of all things”?","options":["נֶכְדָּה","שִׁנּוּי","דַּוְקָא","שָׁבוּעוֹת"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"אֶת ___ קָרָא הַיֶּלֶד.","en":"It was the book the boy read. — fronted for emphasis","options":["בִּכְלָל","הַסֵּפֶר","דַּוְקָא","אֲפִלּוּ"],"correct":1,"full":"אֶת הַסֵּפֶר קָרָא הַיֶּלֶד."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “thus, so”?","options":["לָשׁוֹן","נֵר","כָּךְ","מִתְנַגֵּד"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["גַּם","בִּכְלָל","דַּוְקָא","אֲפִלּוּ"],"correct":3,"say":"אֲפִלּוּ","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["דַּוְקָא","specifically, of all things"],["גַּם","also"],["אֲפִלּוּ","even"],["בִּכְלָל","at all, in general"],["כָּךְ","thus, so"]]},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___ קָרָא אֶת הַסֵּפֶר.","en":"The boy read the book. — ordinary","options":["כָּךְ","דַּוְקָא","הַיֶּלֶד","בִּכְלָל"],"correct":2,"full":"הַיֶּלֶד קָרָא אֶת הַסֵּפֶר."},{"type":"read","he":"גַּם","translit":"gam","en":"also"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “also”?","options":["יְכֹלֶת","הַזֶּה","בַּעַל","גַּם"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"build","tokens":["קָרָא","אֶת","הַסֵּפֶר","הַיֶּלֶד"],"answer":["אֶת","הַסֵּפֶר","קָרָא","הַיֶּלֶד"],"en":"It was the book the boy read. — fronted for emphasis"},{"type":"build","tokens":["קָרָא","הַסֵּפֶר","אֶת","הַיֶּלֶד"],"answer":["הַיֶּלֶד","קָרָא","אֶת","הַסֵּפֶר"],"en":"The boy read the book. — ordinary"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “even” in Hebrew","answer":"אֲפִלּוּ","hint":"afilu"}]}